> I had a similar problem just today.  What I ended up doing is dropping
> all my stuff except my wielded weapon, then walking through the rock,
> and beating the enemy behind it (It was only a Leprachaun).

> I'm no expert in Nethack, but it seemed to work...  is this the best
> thing to do?

Certainly not. Squeezing past a boulder has the risk that a big, nasty
monster may be on the other side, which can beat you to pulp. You may be
armed yourself, but you will certainly have to drop your armour, leaving
you open to attacks, without your armour taking some of the damage.

Also, if you squeeze past a boulder, you lose a point of luck (just like
other ways of "cheating" in Sokoban.

A better way is to pick up some daggers or darts or even some rocks
somewhere, and throw them past the boulder. You may not be able to look
around it; you *are* able to throw that way. Also, spells or wands work
fine, as long as you refrain from wands that destroy the boulder itself,
like force bolt or striking.

